For setting up mraptor services:
* copy mraptord.conf to $HOME/.config/.
  - edit mraptord.conf for your own needs
* copy mraptord.service and ipc.service to /etc/systemd/user/.
* if pkaction --version < 0.106:
    copy 50-mraptor.pkla to /etc/polkit-1/localauthority/50-local.d/.
  else
    copy 50-mraptor.rules to /etc/polkit-1/rules.d
* make mraptord.service and 50-mraptor.rules root:root with permission 0644

* do: 
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    systemctl --user enable ipc.service
    systemctl --user enable mraptord.service
* after that, can start/stop/restart simply with:
    systemctl --user <verb> mraptord.service (no need to start IPC separately)
* you can check if they've started with:
    ps -auxw | grep central
  you should see both central and mraptord running

If more than one person is running on the same machine, you need to change
the port on centralhost variable in mraptord.conf and if your code uses IPC,
change the central port number your own code uses.
